{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_a6275a48eb0609e85c95abf4f965a2d8d57b3ca73827cec28fee0b31c0741a92"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the React Compiler transform cache stores validated {code, map} results via npm cacache under <git-common-dir>/bb-cache/react-compiler, keyed on code, module identity, and a broad toolchain/environment namespace; diagnostics bypass the cache."}],"claim_ids":["clm_a6275a48eb0609e85c95abf4f965a2d8d57b3ca73827cec28fee0b31c0741a92"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_1fd59d48bbe74f40a92f686ba36677e8","id":"pg_87b420966d1750a29ff22dc3ac71b04c","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/get-bb-bb-docs-build-performance-md-d89160eb8c69-2dc3ac71b04c.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_e33a61aa4a4f5f3aa6a682c807131cdf"],"title":"get-bb/bb/docs/build-performance.md @ d89160eb8c69","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1fd59d48bbe74f40a92f686ba36677e8"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_03149061ce175b954a765eb9812c93a1b2e5332d72c5d6378b1ea13e207898a3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"bb is described as an agentic IDE that builds itself, able to control, customize, and automate itself as groundwork for a user's own software factory."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0efd7845d3ff01d2d002f9ba0bccebe9aa818fd937bbb508953280bad32cbdea"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Running via npx serves a web interface at http://localhost:38886."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1b8d88c5987103a1b8a0c523e15d638f6e28e88fc4257a568db691572b353ff6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"bb depends on native add-ons including better-sqlite3, node-pty, and @parcel/watcher built by npm install scripts; npm 12+ blocks those scripts by default, requiring --allow-scripts."},{"claim_ids":["clm_25213cc62ea367d2396d161c7ddace8d5ba299472b47b72c86d52a60a1b957c0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product exposes a desktop app, web app, CLI, and HTTP API as first-class ways to drive bb, with work running in threads that can be followed live, steered, or handed off to another agent."},{"claim_ids":["clm_354d4984d659e3e26d61cbc0cbb5ca300d78fc7efce155f3cb1be644f3299c22"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"bb is in active development: core architecture is described as stable, but workflows and surfaces are still evolving."},{"claim_ids":["clm_38afb1a3663c2af1fb36780d1d2b0dbd8bae3f103a8560031a803831a71d975d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the dev loop uses pnpm dev (Vite with proxied API/WebSocket traffic and per-checkout data dirs under ~/.bb-dev) and pnpm start:worktree to test the production bundle without switching to production data or ports."},{"claim_ids":["clm_85c2c208380e2d11056e49174a13542f6484a6c549b268096fde050148d77fc2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"In remote development modes the server API is unauthenticated and permits command execution and file reads, so the docs instruct restricting access to trusted network boundaries."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c796ccadbdf74a94eb73d209964406eaa036cfa09c8d7c645e7f4dcd2a0231f5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Production runs send anonymous usage telemetry (app starts, thread and message counts, plugin installs) with a random per-install id; development/source runs never send, and BB_TELEMETRY=false opts out."},{"claim_ids":["clm_dcd90f7b77db69dc9b504d015a134812a81bc52a360533c5a829f4b480771666"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is relevant to agent-runtime work: an agentic IDE with plugin/marketplace concepts, a Codex provider plugin adapter, and a published plugin SDK."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f6ff59583867d01f506c74b13ea330fdcb4e4e847eb392d734433507c55011e5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The desktop app supports macOS on Apple Silicon; the Linux x64 AppImage is alpha, Intel Mac users should use npx, and native Windows PowerShell/CMD are unsupported (WSL2 instead)."}],"claim_ids":["clm_03149061ce175b954a765eb9812c93a1b2e5332d72c5d6378b1ea13e207898a3","clm_0efd7845d3ff01d2d002f9ba0bccebe9aa818fd937bbb508953280bad32cbdea","clm_1b8d88c5987103a1b8a0c523e15d638f6e28e88fc4257a568db691572b353ff6","clm_25213cc62ea367d2396d161c7ddace8d5ba299472b47b72c86d52a60a1b957c0","clm_354d4984d659e3e26d61cbc0cbb5ca300d78fc7efce155f3cb1be644f3299c22","clm_38afb1a3663c2af1fb36780d1d2b0dbd8bae3f103a8560031a803831a71d975d","clm_85c2c208380e2d11056e49174a13542f6484a6c549b268096fde050148d77fc2","clm_c796ccadbdf74a94eb73d209964406eaa036cfa09c8d7c645e7f4dcd2a0231f5","clm_dcd90f7b77db69dc9b504d015a134812a81bc52a360533c5a829f4b480771666","clm_f6ff59583867d01f506c74b13ea330fdcb4e4e847eb392d734433507c55011e5"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_1fd59d48bbe74f40a92f686ba36677e8","id":"pg_b379a9446b5751ab96ef6cc5ad829a42","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/get-bb-bb-readme-md-d89160eb8c69-6cc5ad829a42.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_0